[%think 30138] [%out 30608] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 2066] Red's
threats are limited right now. My chariot on h9 attacks the red cannon on h8.
That cannon is guarded only by the red chariot on h6. If the chariot leaves h6
to take g6 (Rxg6), my chariot captures the cannon on h8 for free. Chariot to h7
attacks my horse on g7 and my cannon on i7. My cannon on d7 guards g7, using
the elephant on e7 as its screen, so my cannon on i7 can simply step away. The
real long-term problem is the g6 pawn, which a red horse coming to f4 could
attack. My horse on g7 is also hemmed in. Pushing the pawn from g6 to g5 fixes
both: 1. The pawn on g5 is guarded by the elephant on e7, so it is no longer
exposed. 2. With g6 empty, the horse on g7 can go to f5 or h5, and it still
guards e6 and i6. 3. If Red trades with the g4 pawn and I recapture with the
elephant, my d7 cannon uses the g7 horse as a screen along row 7. A red chariot
landing on h7 would then be captured. 4. If Red plays chariot to h5, my horse
on g7 takes it via h5, since its leg point g6 is now open. 5. If Red plays
chariot to g6, it attacks my horse and pawn, but the h8 cannon is left
unguarded and my chariot takes it. } 15. 兵三进一 象５进７ { [%emt 0:04:16]
